 "name": "seers-chart",
 "about": "The game's own world map (the Adventure map's painting, ui/map/world/01/world01_m.tex, read from the install at runtime and never shipped), cropped to Eorzea [140, 905, 720, 540] and read as a seer's star chart under the moon: the parchment seas in amethyst, the land a shade deeper (a tone on the land mask, x 0.9), the cloud sea's billows in the upper right in sea-green (the second jewel, shaped by the clouds' own lightness and faded at the right wall) and a faint sea-green on the southern sea below the pieces. Each city's banner carries a small star (the lights), and the ley lines Urianger reads are engraved in pale lilac between them: one loop round the five cities and spokes from Mor Dhona (the overlays, where the runtime's glints run). A faint lilac lift over the whole board (a glow of radius 2000) keeps the chart's dark land off sRGB 0-1 (MR 3 round 1, B1). The crop is the first on this texture; the map is the same art as the world painting (-nowloading_base05_hr1) that 3-1 crops, and overlaps 3-1's Aldenard by about two thirds of its area (Ishgard, Gridania and Ala Mhigo are in both).",
